.TH BTK-PRIVKEY 1 "14 August 2026" "Bitcoin Toolkit 4.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
btk-privkey \- create or convert private keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B btk privkey
.B \-\-new
[\fB\-\-count\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-stream\fR]
[\fB\-\-encoding\fR \fIwif\fR|\fIhex\fR|\fIdec\fR]
[\fB\-\-network\fR \fImainnet\fR|\fItestnet\fR]
[\fB\-\-compressed\fR | \fB\-\-uncompressed\fR]
.PP
.B btk privkey
[\fB\-\-encoding\fR \fIwif\fR|\fIhex\fR|\fIdec\fR]
[\fB\-\-network\fR \fImainnet\fR|\fItestnet\fR]
[\fB\-\-compressed\fR | \fB\-\-uncompressed\fR]
[\fB\-\-from\fR \fIwif\fR|\fIhex\fR|\fIdec\fR|\fItext\fR|\fIfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a private key from the CSPRNG, or convert encodings of keys read from
stdin. There are no positional key arguments; pipe the input.
.PP
Without
.B \-\-new
and without
.BR \-\-from ,
each stdin item is guessed as WIF, 64-character hex, or a decimal digit
string. 64-digit all-numeric strings are hex. Anything else is SHA-256'd
as text. Piped binary (NUL, non-text control bytes, or invalid UTF-8) is
hashed whole.
.PP
.B \-\-from
overrides that guess. Use
.B \-\-from text
when the bytes are also a valid key (for example
.BR 1 ).
Use
.B \-\-from file
to hash stdin as raw bytes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-new
CSPRNG key in [1, n\-1]. Generator: does not read stdin.
.TP
.BI \-\-encoding " wif|hex|dec"
Output encoding. Default
.BR wif .
.B dec
is the scalar as a decimal digit string (JSON
.B data
is a string, not a number).
.TP
.BI \-\-network " mainnet|testnet"
Network for generated keys and hex/dec inputs; re-encodes WIF to that
network. Default mainnet.
.TP
.B \-\-compressed
Set the WIF/pubkey compression flag (default).
.TP
.B \-\-uncompressed
Clear the flag. Both flags emit two objects (compressed first).
.TP
.BI \-\-from " wif|hex|dec|text|file"
Force how stdin is interpreted. Default is guess.
.B file
hashes the entire stream (one key).
.B text
SHA-256s each line. This is not a KDF.
.TP
.BI \-\-count " N"
With
.BR \-\-new ,
emit N keys. N must be a positive integer.
.TP
.B \-\-stream
With
.BR \-\-new ,
emit until SIGINT. Combined with
.B \-\-count N
emits exactly N.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " ndjson|json|plain"
Output framing. Default ndjson.
.TP
.BI \-\-in " auto|ndjson|json|plain"
Stdin framing. Default auto. Ignored for
.BR "\-\-from file" .
.SH NOTES
.B \-\-new
and
.B \-\-from
cannot be combined. SHA-256 of a passphrase is not a KDF.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR btk (1)
